{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488738-who-is-yama-king-shau-yar-han","id":1488738,"title":"Who is Yama King Shau-yar Han?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-01T15:22:52-07:00","id":1488738,"title":"Who is Yama King Shau-yar Han?","content":"I've seen the Yama King Shau-yar Han briefly mentioned in several of the Kindred of the East books, but I can't find any solid info on him. What I can find mentions that Tou Mu placed the ideas about the Outer Ones into Shau-yar Han's mind, which led him to madness, and that to prevent Yomi from being ripped asunder from within, the other Yama Kings were forced to destroy him. Anyone know more about Shau-yar Han or the Outer Ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T15:49:04-07:00","id":1488739,"title":"","content":"It's most likely a throwaway line meant for flavour. So you can do to it whatever you like. I don't see anything significant in Heresies of the Way, Thousand Hells or Dark Kingdom of Jade.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T15:58:56-07:00","id":1488741,"title":"","content":"I remember asking that years and years ago and got no response. I think that like Asmodai said, it's a throwaway line.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T16:09:58-07:00","id":1488743,"title":"","content":"Well the Outer Ones are probably like Cthulhu Mythos type beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T17:26:55-07:00","id":1488748,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I think it's safe to assume that the &quot;Outer Ones&quot; are the same &quot;Outer Lords&quot; that the K'llasshaa Nephandi worship. They're basically the White Wolf version of the Outer Gods of the Cthulhu Mythos.<br /> <br /> *edit* Now that I think about it, I seem to recall that in one of the optional Ascension scenarios it says that the Outer Lords are, in fact, simply the dreams of the Neverborn in the Labyrinth. When the Neverborn start to wake up, the Outer Lords begin to vanish and their servants are suddenly left powerless. It's been a long time since I read that and don't remember if that was canon or just one of those options in a single scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-01-2022, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-01T17:58:14-07:00","id":1488750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1488738-who-is-yama-king-shau-yar-han?p=1488748#post1488748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I think it's safe to assume that the &quot;Outer Ones&quot; are the same &quot;Outer Lords&quot; that the K'llasshaa Nephandi worship. They're basically the White Wolf version of the Outer Gods of the Cthulhu Mythos.<br /> <br /> *edit* Now that I think about it, I seem to recall that in one of the optional Ascension scenarios it says that the Outer Lords are, in fact, simply the dreams of the Neverborn in the Labyrinth. When the Neverborn start to wake up, the Outer Lords begin to vanish and their servants are suddenly left powerless. It's been a long time since I read that and don't remember if that was canon or just one of those options in a single scenario.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I remember reading that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T19:23:07-07:00","id":1489042,"title":"","content":"That's not in the Ascension book, it was Mage Revised's position on the beings the Nephandi served. I'm not sure if the take first showed up in the core or the Revised Book of Madness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-03T20:24:04-07:00","id":1489051,"title":"","content":"I first saw that in 1997's Book of Mirrors (the Mage Storytellers Guide). However, I don't think it's limited to the Outer Lords of the K'llasshaa. It's <i>all</i> the entities that all the Nephandi worship which includes the Demons Lords of Infernalists and the mightiest beings of Malfeas serving the Wyrm. It appears at that time the game was stating that the Neverborn Malfeans of the Labyrinth were what was objectively &quot;real&quot; in the metaphysics of the World of Darkness, and all the other various entities of prime evil in the setting were derived from them.<br /> <br /> The evidence was that when Neverborn Malfean Gorool woke up in 1994, all the Nephandi fighting the Traditions and Technocracy in WoD's version of WWII suddenly lost many of their allies and powers.<br /> <br /> I thought it was actually quite a clever way to eat your cake and have it too in regards to the various competing entities of evil based on various human culture and supernatural creatures' own myths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}